(8. HEADER ANALYSIS \(3 PACKETS\)) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(Packets analyzed: Frame 1, Frame 4, Frame 6.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(1. Why is TTL not zero?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - TTL is initialized by sender \(64 here\) and decremented per router hop. On) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     loopback \(`127.0.0.1`\), packets do not traverse routers, so TTL remains 64) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     and never reaches zero.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(2. Why do packet sizes differ?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - Different TCP segments carry different payload/control content. For example,) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     SYN packets are 60 bytes, pure ACK packets are 52 bytes, and packets with) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     payload \(`PSH,ACK`\) can be 54 or 60 bytes.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(3. What information does protocol field provide?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - It identifies the transport protocol carried by IP. Here `PROTOCOL_NO=6`) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     means TCP.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(4. What could happen if protocol field is modified?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - The receiver/network stack may pass the packet to the wrong protocol) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     handler, causing parsing failure or packet drop.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(5. What do protocol-specific fields reveal?) Tj
0 -14 Td
(   - TCP source/destination ports identify flow endpoints, and TCP flags reveal) Tj
0 -14 Td
(     connection phase \(SYN handshake, ACK confirmation, PSH data, FIN close\).) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(9. PROGRAM ENHANCEMENT) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
ET
endstream
